cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt BORA-EAI, please cite it as below."
title: "Business Outcome Risk Analysis for Enterprise AI (BORA-EAI)"
version: "0.1"
date-released: 2026-11-10
license: CC-BY-4.0
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Generative Security"
    website: "https://generativesecurity.ai"
  - family-names: "Wasielewski"
    given-names: "Michael"
    name-suffix: "Jr."
    affiliation: "Generative Security"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Generative-Security"
abstract: >-
  An open model for analyzing the risk of how an enterprise uses AI at the business-outcome
  level. BORA-EAI takes the AI use case as the unit of analysis, runs it through nine layers,
  draws on a library of fifteen business threat scenarios with one accountable executive each, and
  nets risk-adjusted value against expected loss and governance cost as a range.
keywords:
  - "AI risk"
  - "risk analysis"
  - "threat modeling"
  - "enterprise risk management"
  - "AI governance"
  - "CISO"
